From: ZHOU YUXIN <zhou.yuxin@u.nus.edu>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:21:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] Add related-items recommendation and the browse history
 behind it

Sprint 2, WP5.

The Sprint 1 frontend already calls /api/recommendations/products/{id}/similar,
/api/recommendations/for-you and /api/history/view. None of those endpoints
existed. All three calls are wrapped in a catch that only writes to the
console, so the sections simply rendered empty and nothing reported a fault.
This adds the backend they were written against.

Three rules decide what gets shown, each because breaking it is visible on the
page:

- the item being viewed is never in its own related list, which would be a
  link back to itself
- delisted items and items whose stock is entirely held by unpaid orders are
  filtered out, so the strip cannot advertise something unbuyable
- a category with nothing left falls back to recent listings rather than
  leaving an empty strip under a heading that promised content

/for-you is deliberately shallow this sprint: the categories the user has
browsed, and recent listings for anyone without history. The cold-start
branching and the personalised algorithm are Sprint 5 - this just stops the
home feed calling an endpoint that is not there.

6 more tests, 41 in total.
